From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:34:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Mac: a Home menu on a short press, and a game paused in the
 background

Many controllers switch off when Home is held, so the 2 s hold to quit is
the only way back from a game and often does not work. A short press of
Home (let go within 0.5 s) now opens a Home menu over the game, on the
quit prompt's card: Resume, Back to console mode and Quit. Up and down
(d-pad or left stick) choose, A selects, B or a new press of Home resumes.
Quit opens the existing quit prompt, so ending the game is asked first.
The game is out of focus and gets no controller input while the menu is
open, as with the prompt. The hold keeps opening the quit prompt.

Back to console mode is shown only with DM_HOME_MENU_LAUNCHER=1, which a
launcher sets for a game started from its console mode. It pauses the
game as a minimized window is paused (input released, focus 3, audio and
graphics suspended), leaves full screen, hands the activation to the app
named by DM_LAUNCHER_BUNDLE_ID and hides the game. The game resumes as a
restored window does when it is active again, and on the distributed
notification org.nxnative.resume.<pid>. org.nxnative.quit.<pid> quits it
through NSApp terminate. It posts org.nxnative.paused.<pid> and
org.nxnative.resumed.<pid>, and logs "front end: paused in the background"
and "front end: resumed". DM_HOME_MENU=0 turns the menu off.

home_quit.h gets the menu and the paused phase (hq_step_nav with up and
down, hq_resumed). DM_HOME_QUIT_TEXT takes three more lines after the
five it has: Resume, Back to console mode and the menu's title.

Tests: t_home_quit.c (short press and hold told apart, the menu off, the
rows with and without the launcher's, moving and clamping, Resume, Back to
console mode and resuming from it, Quit asking first), t_home_quit_mac.m
(the menu's view), t_controllers_mac.m (up and down from a native pad),
test_env_switches.py and test_docs.py.

Front-ends: new: DM_HOME_MENU_LAUNCHER=1 and DM_LAUNCHER_BUNDLE_ID give a Mac game a Back to console mode row that pauses it in the background, org.nxnative.resume.<pid> and org.nxnative.quit.<pid> control it, org.nxnative.paused.<pid> and org.nxnative.resumed.<pid> report it
Front-ends: new: DM_HOME_QUIT_TEXT takes three more lines (Resume, Back to console mode, the menu title)

Upstream-Status: pending [seedds/nxnative#TBD, becomes forwarded when the PR is open]
Reason: A Home menu on a short press of Home, and a game paused in the background for the launcher's console mode
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#952

